{"boundary":"Configured source-text signatures, not elaborated Lean or a complete dependency context. Truncation and unresolved names are explicit; full definitions and source remain on demand.","contributions":[{"author":{"kind":"agent","name":"Codex source review 1"},"body":"The captured configured assertion and the cited paper assertion were read with their relevant definitions; the disclosed relation follows the stated scope, not the previous frontend choice.\n\nInspected: Read all three sharpness conjuncts, including k≥3, lifetime exponent k/(k−1), q1 lower scale and the replacement-error limit.\n\nCapture rebinding by Codex, 26 October 2026: the Atlas capture revision changed after an outside-report wording correction. The pinned Lean text, configuration, paper text and proposed relation are unchanged; no new review is implied.","content_sha256":"sha256:fd5a51d8f0d4cf94414ca4df149d2f51fc9dca79463dc0c5b788d5cc3804899e","fingerprint":"sha256:335659b57c97866bc7ee1c75bc0f2141122412776fbe58139402be61e79a26c1","kind":"statement-link","license":"Apache-2.0","navigation":{"decision":"linked","limitations":"Agent source reading; no human approval, Lean replay or whole-statement equivalence certificate. The captured configured assertion and the cited paper assertion were read with their relevant definitions; the disclosed relation follows the stated scope, not the previous frontend choice.","schema":"statement-map-navigation-reading/1","source_sha256":"sha256:ee5a15059201018a11142484b06e5475ff636df59b3f5a449fde9d60190f1593","targets":[{"declarations":["OAI.RandomKSAT.sharpness"],"explanation":"The first sharpness conjunct constructs arbitrarily large instances violating any proposed lifetime exponent γ<k/(k−1), with the stated q1 lower scale. This is the paper’s lifetime-sharpness proposition and is one conjunct of the configured combined theorem.","fingerprint":"sha256:c22e531f0745d5bfb2920bcbfa7acb83120c9232e2c988cfa40741df3d8acb3e","limitations":"The replacement-error assertions are separate conjuncts and require the other linked proposition.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Variance-of-the-Random-k-SAT-Hitting-Time-September-27-2026#prop:lifetime-sharp","statement_sha256":"sha256:f6598e01e5b7c344cb5ed97942f652015ea148e9aa05ef009bbece482c794536"},{"declarations":["OAI.RandomKSAT.sharpness"],"explanation":"The remaining conjuncts give a sequence with q1−R_g asymptotic to 2^−k g^(−(k−1)) and rule out a uniform little-o replacement error. These match the paper’s replacement-sharpness proposition.","fingerprint":"sha256:9b9c4e9fd8ef2bb3e5b41bcee3fd00f7eae2e79909230ab6bc3c211f1ec2ee0d","limitations":"This proposition does not by itself cover the lifetime exponent assertion; the two links jointly identify the inspected conjunction.","relation":"paper-is-part","row_id":"Variance-of-the-Random-k-SAT-Hitting-Time-September-27-2026#prop:replacement-sharp","statement_sha256":"sha256:6554719f725070ada91f5a9965150fe872ec5bce2365eceafe5c645cd5d58fad"}]},"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","provenance":{"identity_assurance":"named local attestation; identity not independently authenticated","kind":"agent-drafted-unreviewed"},"references":["https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/SATSharpness.lean","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Variance-of-the-Random-k-SAT-Hitting-Time-September-27-2026/build/source/sections/replacement-sharpness.tex#L64","https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/Variance-of-the-Random-k-SAT-Hitting-Time-September-27-2026/build/source/sections/replacement-sharpness.tex#L129"],"release_id":"openai-math","review_state":"unreviewed","row_id":"challenge:SATSharpness","schema":"statement-map-contribution/1"}],"detail":{"path":"lean/4a8b4a313af8cf7d22c0e9bd.json","pointer":""},"formal_statement":{"detail":{"path":"lean/4a8b4a313af8cf7d22c0e9bd.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/4a8b4a313af8cf7d22c0e9bd.json","pointer":"/reader/formal_statement"},"kind":"declaration-signatures","method":"configured-challenge-declaration-signatures","name_resolution":"source-text","snippets":[{"complete":true,"detail":{"path":"lean/4a8b4a313af8cf7d22c0e9bd.json","pointer":"/reader/selected_statements/0"},"full_source":{"path":"lean/4a8b4a313af8cf7d22c0e9bd.json","pointer":"/challenge/lean"},"name":"OAI.RandomKSAT.sharpness","source":{"file":"lean/ComparatorChallenges/SATSharpness.lean","line":58,"pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","sha256":"ee5a15059201018a11142484b06e5475ff636df59b3f5a449fde9d60190f1593","statement_sha256":"sha256:0916fbb2b5079e25e4f4770e0babfe23afb5918b70de7c7765d1b24e7b4871c8","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/lean/ComparatorChallenges/SATSharpness.lean#L58"},"text":"theorem sharpness (k : ℕ) (hk : 3 ≤ k) :\n    (∀ γ D A : ℝ, γ < (k : ℝ) / ((k-1 : ℕ) : ℝ) → 0 < D → 0 < A →\n      ∀ N : ℕ, ∃ u : ℕ, N ≤ u ∧ k ≤ u ∧ ∃ S : Finset (Assignment u),\n        S.Nonempty ∧ A * (u : ℝ) ^ (-((k-1 : ℕ) : ℝ)) ≤ blockKill u (k-1) S 1 ∧\n        D * (blockKill u (k-1) S 1) ^ (-γ) < lifetime u k S) ∧\n    (∃ u : ℕ → ℕ, ∃ S : ∀ g, Finset (Assignment (u g)),\n      (∀ g, 2 ≤ g → k ≤ u g ∧ (S g).Nonempty) ∧\n      Asymptotics.IsEquivalent Filter.atTop\n        (fun g => blockKill (u g) (k-1) (S g) 1 - blockKill (u g) k (S g) g)\n        (fun g => ((2 : ℝ)^k)⁻¹ * (g : ℝ)^(-((k-1 : ℕ) : ℝ)))) ∧\n    (¬ ∃ e : ℕ → ℝ,\n      Asymptotics.IsLittleO Filter.atTop e (fun g => (g : ℝ)^(-((k-1 : ℕ) : ℝ))) ∧\n      ∀ u, k ≤ u → ∀ S : Finset (Assignment u), S.Nonempty → ∀ g, 2 ≤ g →\n        blockKill u (k-1) S 1 - e g ≤ blockKill u k S g)"}],"state":"available","unresolved_names":[]},"generation_id":"sha256:fda4c3462963b650c538e2177794811eb1c221b267efea4b091fd6e397533f81","id":"l:SATSharpness","kind":"lean-preview","omissions":[],"pairings":{"f: